<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:09:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: Merz calls for Korean reunification at DMZ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1657f82eb8166ac50f7a5c00a85517f6aec531b7520465d7be676377335ac0da</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-calls-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462--aab86da9bea8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-calls-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has expressed hope for Korean reunification during a visit to the heavily fortified border. Meanwhile, President Steinmeier has held talks with China's Xi Jinping in Beijing. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Seoul fears being sidelined as US reaches out to North Korea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cd421d63ebfc08d47358f75801bed9ffb67b7276e4976097529faf9ed925679</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/seoul-fears-being-sidelined-as-us-reaches-out-to-north-korea/a-79808098--b371be6c550b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/seoul-fears-being-sidelined-as-us-reaches-out-to-north-korea/a-79808098?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With ties between South Korea and the Trump administration strained, the South Korean government worries that Donald Trump's pursuit of a diplomatic breakthrough with Kim Jong Un may come at Seoul's expense.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d6a3229f094a3b38bfc56245d4268365dff1d07510a4146141a0f6c606a8a1e</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Kenya friendly highlights Africa's growing pull for global sport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b9f2393f67f1d880b27571f1960feda024f7eb6869147151e69e7620017d3a1</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753--c6f4b50cf1c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich are to open Nairobi's new Raila Odinga International Stadium against Ajax as Kenya prepares for AFCON 2027. The match highlights Africa's growing sports ambitions — and questions over cost and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Italy: Students and workers rally over living costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4deb89143614f9395d29bf49e004950d900ee7c6e040cf58072eed2c7fd33862</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-students-and-workers-rally-over-living-costs/a-79807668--a510f9e16fc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-students-and-workers-rally-over-living-costs/a-79807668?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students and workers have marched across Italy for more school funding and relief from rising living costs. The rallies follow weeks of school occupations and protests against higher military spending.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Binance crypto exchange suspends trades over North Korea-linked hack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5df43c00a31c7404f45b5aa421eaec6b585e9e289ed0ea59ca0795a50386ee9c</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/binance-crypto-exchange-suspends-trades-over-north-korea-linked-hack/a-79803280--a05325fd4819.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/binance-crypto-exchange-suspends-trades-over-north-korea-linked-hack/a-79803280?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Crypto platform Binance has suspended trading following a suspected hack now linked to North Korea. The disruption has left users unable to trade on the cryptocurrency platform while the suspected breach is investigated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany takes cautious approach on Israeli election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba0ed2294eb50102031aced8ae3f04bac8c055e3687af17d5dab9c3c848a36f2</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184--6eb977f23eb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German politicians have been slow to respond as they wait to see who is likely to comprise the next coalition. Many are also hoping for a government without religious hardliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Critical newspaper 'Novaya Gazeta' to close</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83ec90410cf9ea20c50af0ff4aeb8e2bfe15d6698769e26b8c7f32938c499940</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-critical-newspaper-novaya-gazeta-to-close/a-79805693--37cf795ba96d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-critical-newspaper-novaya-gazeta-to-close/a-79805693?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"Novaya Gazeta," one of the last remaining independent, critical media outlets in Russia, has announced it is closing under pressure from state authorities. Meanwhile, in Ukraine, evacuations have begun in Oleshky.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's new anti-gang law: Can it curb organized crime?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d8175ae324200916335967b0de0db87339026cd789edb14325951b7d21aa138</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-new-anti-gang-law-can-it-curb-organized-crime/a-79799450--d75f18b5acf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-new-anti-gang-law-can-it-curb-organized-crime/a-79799450?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A tough stance against organized crime? One year after a massacre that left more than 130 people dead, a new law aims to crack down on drug cartels in Rio's favelas.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>IIHF ordered to allow Russia back into world championships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c27da3d767d3bb53ccda87a5edc96d10e73aa2746622ae784d04f330095a0bac</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650--8e19bd1daa6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has ruled that Russian teams must be allowed to take part in international ice hockey tournaments. The IIHF had banned Russia following the country's full-scale invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Many Turkish 'guest workers' hit by poverty in old age</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b11531481bd091c83138884259d30078a52007e9de336a22ac3a1ede62e532e1</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/many-turkish-guest-workers-hit-by-poverty-in-old-age/a-79746838--0d5019a9af26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/many-turkish-guest-workers-hit-by-poverty-in-old-age/a-79746838?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">West Germany and Turkey signed an agreement allowing the temporary recruitment of workers on October 30, 1961. Sixty-five years on, many so-called 'guest workers' can't live from their pensions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The dachshund, a humorous icon with political symbolism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13b937bb4a2d4f2d263aeff82269d103c2dba26f2bf78ddda41e2a8fd58b6e80</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:08:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191--0ec0144d606e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Picasso to Andy Warhol, a surprising number of artists have portrayed the German breed. But the dachshund has also at times been co-opted as a political symbol.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Space agency to boost GPS alternative with new satellite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab0d5fedd64be8fd576c556a2348218619d6d2a06c8c9d0b4d81ec91daa9def4</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:09:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T06:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-space-agency-to-boost-gps-alternative-with-new-satellite/live-79803564--d1c7d69799ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-space-agency-to-boost-gps-alternative-with-new-satellite/live-79803564?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Indian national space agency's mission aims to strengthen its indigenous navigation system and reduce reliance on the US-owned GPS. Meanwhile, Rahul Gandhi renewed his call for more election protests. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: Netanyahu, main rival fall short of majority after all votes counted</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e32320c74b921a70dfda7fa00a251977abca04e358fbfc57369d4f576bb72dd</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T06:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-election-netanyahu-main-rival-fall-short-of-majority-after-all-votes-counted/live-79713839--123e742eecd2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-election-netanyahu-main-rival-fall-short-of-majority-after-all-votes-counted/live-79713839?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With all the votes counted, the pro-Netanyahu bloc finished ahead of Gadi Eisenkot's anti-Netanyahu bloc. But tough coalition talks loom as neither grouping won a majority. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela: Opposition leader Maria Corina Machado says US backs 2027 election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d1517bf5a2bc6ad122d9fb2721dc45ec18d2343bee53baeb16f3f1d3e752b39</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T03:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/venezuela-opposition-leader-maria-corina-machado-says-us-backs-2027-election/a-79803426--79d168103188.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/venezuela-opposition-leader-maria-corina-machado-says-us-backs-2027-election/a-79803426?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The return of Maria Corina Machado, who says Trump opened the "floodgate to freedom" for Venezuela, presents a challenge for Washington as Trump has also backed interim President Delcy Rodriguez.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayer wins Roundup cancer trial after Supreme Court ruling</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d96a972322701a43c4a788db9bd27a8f56044c585aa39c41f05731f851a2f6c</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T02:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayer-wins-roundup-cancer-trial-after-supreme-court-ruling/a-79803301--b3d21555ad34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayer-wins-roundup-cancer-trial-after-supreme-court-ruling/a-79803301?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The weedkiller Roundup has been accused of being carcinogenic to humans despite no warning on its label. Bayer is seeking to settle tens of thousands of further cases.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Alexander Zverev clinches tennis No. 1 ranking</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4942d178e0f7e12b3438ef380396fea2b54bc51054bb87cf6b2186f0971718cf</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T22:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048--1b03a09b61b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev is the second German man, after Boris Becker, to clinch the No. 1 spot in tennis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Star Trek' star Patrick Stewart dies age 86</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1c34a16215bcb33e7e08b398e27f1f6e3098564cf2c2c3e257d44eb30df270</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T22:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/star-trek-star-patrick-stewart-dies-age-86/a-79803071--53b89389ae81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/star-trek-star-patrick-stewart-dies-age-86/a-79803071?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Shakespearean actor landed the role of a lifetime as "Star Trek" Captain Picard. He passed away at age 86.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Justice for Maya women in Guatemala, girls back in school in India, restored land in Mali: The UN has named its 2026 SDG Action Award winners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1272cd023733d5dd9ccf770b29f49fe2ed0d858da6ff869e41d8dca9cb65b538</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/justice-for-maya-women-in-guatemala-girls-back-in-school-in-india-restored-land-in-mali-the-un-has-n/a-79801727--31a109934113.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/justice-for-maya-women-in-guatemala-girls-back-in-school-in-india-restored-land-in-mali-the-un-has-named-its-2026-sdg-action-award-winners/a-79801727?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Champions of indigenous women's rights in Guatemala, girls' education in India, and restored farmland in Mali all featured among the winners of UN's SDG Action Awards.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin's Elif Eralp under fire over Der Spiegel interview</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42d4aa6f9b24b30daaf91efa0afe7b116661fab53118d27ffe6285bcd75a7788</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T20:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-elif-eralp-under-fire-over-der-spiegel-interview/a-79799766--cde8b7af3fbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-s-elif-eralp-under-fire-over-der-spiegel-interview/a-79799766?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Left candidate Elif Eralp has sparked controversy after Der Spiegel reported she was advised against mentioning a pro-Palestinian activist for fear of reprisals against her family.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India increases growth forecast for fiscal year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8460e35d4ea5d41bd70d5a1aff571a6692fca24b708858c78238dac67ca07047</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971--fa1e5ffdabbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Ministry of Finance has increased its growth forecasts for the current fiscal year. But it also warned about inflation, particularly for fuel and energy, amid continued instability in the Middle East.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany seeks new head of state</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98ac301b9608495b7e1730e87bd852277225b88362485a3b6640d4879aba2b10</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-seeks-new-head-of-state/a-79797794--10071c049ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-seeks-new-head-of-state/a-79797794?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The question of who should become Germany's new presiden is becoming pressing. Many want to see Germany's first female head of state. Chancellor Friedrich Merz is keeping his cards close to his chest.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen logs Q3 operating loss of €5.86 billion on Porsche writedown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11a7dd8b88bd4e850f2d5e7eb233f9022fbbdd3a35f4fea24b7f970ce7d584fd</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-_5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796--74f8be5771cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-€5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Volkswagen Group has filed its worst quarterly performance since the height of the "Dieselgate" scandal in 2015. Share prices climbed in response, however, perhaps because the bad news was so well signposted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US moves to lift sanctions on Russia's shadow fleet could undermine Western pressure on Moscow and help fund its war in Ukraine.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b33b9afba91b5d43fa44ea6b36a2b7b0da5d9899e73a820cbba985d55c7eb00a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-moves-to-lift-sanctions-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet-could-undermine-western-pressure-on-moscow-and-h/a-79787035--48ad80b5a4bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-moves-to-lift-sanctions-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet-could-undermine-western-pressure-on-moscow-and-help-fund-its-war-in-ukraine/a-79787035?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is reportedly considering ways to convert "dark tankers" into legitimate vessels, allowing them to transport crude oil that is not subject to sanctions.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Chancellor Friedrich Merz accuses North Korea of threatening Europe's freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66348fce713c782995514ef329cf38265fb995d7bfa38041ad8e1b823a03a1ad</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-chancellor-friedrich-merz-accuses-north-korea-of-threatening-europe-s-freedom/live-79792915--91e1e32cf271.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-chancellor-friedrich-merz-accuses-north-korea-of-threatening-europe-s-freedom/live-79792915?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Friedrich Merz, who is visiting Seoul, said North Korea is putting Europe's security at risk by sending soldiers to fight for Russia in Ukraine. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European Central Bank (ECB) head Christine Lagarde to step down in February, before her term ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97cb14e5da0577de07e73db1f7738fe89997104a0633c2ab4c4e1796570c1106</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-central-bank-ecb-head-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-before-her-term-ends/a-79794353--c27511a3878b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-central-bank-ecb-head-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-before-her-term-ends/a-79794353?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Central Bank (ECB) President Christine Lagarde is to resign nine months ahead of the end of her 8-year term. European Council President Antonio Costa has said the process to find a successor is underway.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich head coach Vincent Kompany's health scare highlights the need for better support for elite coaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1d1b2da441ad8faf5a677034d3d1673e461d83b6f8e0648b73c144a746212ba</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-e/a-79764661--fcbaed2aac2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-elite-coaches/a-79764661?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vincent Kompany’s health concern is a reminder that elite football's pressures affect coaches too. Better support, clearer structures and mental health safeguards are increasingly vital.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Evacuation from Oleshky: How are preparations going?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a44c692c020da6876a5a45a0493d3417cbc679afc212d90e2372173176ec658</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/evacuation-from-oleshky-how-are-preparations-going/a-79790001--e77f75613f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/evacuation-from-oleshky-how-are-preparations-going/a-79790001?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A lawyer with the Save Ukraine Foundation, Myroslava Kharchenko, told DW about what has been happening in Russian-occupied Oleshky since a temporary ceasefire brokered by Melania Trump took effect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests in Germany: Is France-style violence looming?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:959e454b2693391d0085d43e70877ac63c9b1269f37fdd452061bcba45168980</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050--fb575275c7ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Young people in Germany are preparing to protest over education and climate change. Politicians fear violence like in France, but an expert sees differences.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Can we regrow damaged seagrass meadows?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ee7fef3ef55ed0d11d69e03a7284a83ce87123a04fb91902738c07ebf325380</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925--ee57fe9c850d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seagrass protects coasts, shelters thousands of species and stores CO2. But some 30% of this valuable ecosystem has disappeared since the late 19th century. Can we bring it back?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>EU's 'Made in Europe' push unnerves global auto suppliers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45432750df5b068f2a75a51440f68024718d48b7088c180325bf30155627d030</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579--7391c1bc1a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In shielding Europe's carmakers from Chinese rivals, the EU risks hurting close partners from Turkey and Morocco to Japan and South Korea. Billions in trade and hundreds of thousands of European jobs are at stake.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Russia in Africa: What is Putin hoping to achieve?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aef485c1508eaef102a983d665af2704337939471b2aef002497f9b0c6bdab32</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858--24074440aebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its invasion of Ukraine and the resulting rift with the West, Russia has declared that it intends to make a "historic return" to Africa. What have we seen of this so far?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's first Youth Olympics open in Senegal amid hope and scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72b1bf1683d52e367061f8c1f23c0ce284859fe7b92a80d858ba7b7b1d6825a4</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478--c3155dbcff43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senegal is hosting Africa's first Youth Olympics, with 2,700 young athletes competing in Dakar, Diamniadio and Saly. The Games bring pride and hope, but also questions over cost, rights and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian police shoot dead assailant at Israeli Embassy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c79be0819512c13b7743112b2d8ad8a4ab84f7571850573f79d25c4b3a98f5c7</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905--d152a4aa69fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A "minor" has been killed by police after attacking a guard at Israel's embassy in Belgrade with knives, the interior minister says. Ivica Dacic said police had declared the highest terror alert after the incident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:352d2a12cabe25b939c7c6f521c12d497ea8719e8af541e2dec4cab30393d898</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane has won football's most prestigious individual prize, beating Kylian Mbappe and Lamine Yamal. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz says erosion of global order means middle powers in Europe and Asia must be more assertive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55030bbfe215cbdc58b2a3f61fd0c65bddf6ee86becf8f62f64347fb6433791a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-says-erosion-of-global-order-means-middle-powers-in-europe-and-asia-must-be-more-asse/live-79772992--98272a034e7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-says-erosion-of-global-order-means-middle-powers-in-europe-and-asia-must-be-more-assertive/live-79772992?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During a visit to Singapore, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said Europe and Germany want to increase free trade with open competition, reliability and a rules-based order.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>England and Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane wins Ballon d'Or</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92de24893868b1ff579a6082d320b11ce680b6842428e2226f1b69f1ab1c9ac8</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/england-and-bayern-munich-striker-harry-kane-wins-ballon-d-or/a-79771067--21e06316b487.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/england-and-bayern-munich-striker-harry-kane-wins-ballon-d-or/a-79771067?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The England captain ends his country's 25-year wait for the prestigious award after scoring 73 goals for club and country last season, beating competition from Lamine Yamal and Kylian Mbappe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What Germany thinks of carmaker Audi's $4 billion deal with Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebafe2957efdeb214767f28c4476ad404b1782d6a4999c685c67d881c8f8b97b</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-germany-thinks-of-carmaker-audi-s-4-billion-deal-with-trump/a-79760479--6c6f86b95e86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-germany-thinks-of-carmaker-audi-s-4-billion-deal-with-trump/a-79760479?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The luxury carmaker is set to open its first factory in the United States — a move Trump credits to his tariffs. DW examines the German reaction amid a massive auto industry cull at home.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Steinmeier in China: A major state visit in uncertain times</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd5a080d6e95d64f3c89763a7bef7b56a8372f063cc15ee671a5a1386a41ad9e</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/steinmeier-in-china-a-major-state-visit-in-uncertain-times/a-79764205--23bd9ee47a5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/steinmeier-in-china-a-major-state-visit-in-uncertain-times/a-79764205?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Frank-Walter Steinmeier is traveling to China on a state visit in a period of political and economic uncertainty. Germany is seeking alternative partners in the region but also wants good ties with Beijing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>From rotten food to political opponents: Researchers explore how disgust relates to our beliefs, and why the connection is complicated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7790a680108b0d8bae4d64df2b01b7e2c4dd02587b2c8bad71c81b05358e696a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-w/a-79734659--e9b7cd7e436d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-why-the-connection-is-complicated/a-79734659?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some studies have linked disgust sensitivity to socially conservative attitudes. But ahead of the US midterm elections, does disgust shape our politics, or do our beliefs shape what we find disgusting?</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested after nationwide protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fefbc86fddbbe2c224f8e00d33ed2a2cf2b718f926877f7d191da5ea3e77ec29</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protests-more-violence-feared-amid-renewed-demonstrations/live-79748223--43db314a2270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-after-nationwide-protests/live-79748223?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The French government says more than 1,000 people were arrested following nationwide protests on Saturday. Police and elite security forces were out in force across the country as clashes broke out.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Prague honors Roma resistance fighters against Hitler</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:619e106b9ef3bb682f3901af11a7d2a9f475485d11598c064f58079726c095d0</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/prague-honors-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015--c9d68b8992df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/prague-honors-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 1,400 Roma fought against the German Nazi occupation in Czechoslovakia. A new exhibition in Prague showcases the stories of partisans and soldiers whose fates barely received any attention for decades.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Bulgaria, record low voter turnout triggers a November 1 presidential run-off in a poll colored by divisions over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a144365004e2efc6bf495af166c61d1d502d312633f26b9a541d29810537349</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-bulgaria-record-low-voter-turnout-triggers-a-november-1-presidential-run-off-in-a-poll-colored-by/a-79753496--78ae87f6d8b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-bulgaria-record-low-voter-turnout-triggers-a-november-1-presidential-run-off-in-a-poll-colored-by-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Low voter turnout has triggered a run-off for the Bulgarian presidency. The vote was colored by strong divisions over Russia's war in Ukraine, and Sofia's relations with the Kremlin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's new deal on Mediterranean maritime boundaries with Libya is exacerbating issues with Greece and the EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5b336f7d5867547bf4897660e70bf56d454237f5c5874a7c3247500114cf0f5</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece/a-79745971--8e4f859a6229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece-and-the-eu/a-79745971?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey and Libya plan to redraw maritime boundaries in the Mediterranean as part of a new economic corridor. This has sparked strong protests from Greece, and has also drawn the European Union into the conflict.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4027f39c77701bf285de416f545548c09447fdcea618ee29bea25b3f114e0186</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's attacks on Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, are intensifying. DW asked people on the ground what life is like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:948a761a4fe512b9abc24bbb6f1cf7a542ba33291593520887f3be6e4cc61816</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-/a-79741090--9d6ca1b7b337.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-is-like/a-79741090?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's attacks on the Ukrainian capital are hitting harder and more frequently, making 2026 one of the long war's bloodiest years for Kyiv. DW asked people on the ground what life is like.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine tries to shut Moscow's airports with drone strikes on Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4322c4cb4b78a618d7046a2d94f46ea1bab98efcfe84207acf609a66d50f565f</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469--16f9cb7db516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Repeated Ukrainian drone attacks are increasingly disrupting operations at Moscow's airports. The pounding is part of Ukraine's plan to shut down Russia's airpace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: Hope, tension and apprehension as voters prepare to elect new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f63d27ab3f9c21f01cf1c2851eccff10ef7b5ab9e466aef6d39abdacccd4df73</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-hope-tension-and-apprehension-as-voters-prepare-to-elect-new-parliament/a-79738102--35e507b36c9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-hope-tension-and-apprehension-as-voters-prepare-to-elect-new-parliament/a-79738102?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two years of protests, Serbia faces a pivotal election on Sunday, with a student-led challenge to Aleksandar Vucic's lengthy rule. Allegations of electoral irregularities and fears of a post-election crisis abound.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sit out FIFA Under-15 World Cup as Russia return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:766ebac1791e6155a1e21f549b5e593d7e411a23432629025c4f104d66c4dd65</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T07:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sit-out-fifa-under-15-world-cup-as-russia-return/a-79734040--d1c93bdcd718.html" type="tex