nt protests are only getting bigger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64c3e4e505b401c5b6e981784260af84818412dca1a8b0b21f0957a01e3884e2</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T19:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-s-student-protests-are-only-getting-bigger/a-79735213--609bd8634d9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-s-student-protests-are-only-getting-bigger/a-79735213?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As police try to suppress anti-corruption protests by young Albanians, Prime Minister Edi Rama is claiming that "antifa" is behind the unrest. Few are buying that explanation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Are the French police the most violent in the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c892ec63a9a95d782aaabc31ddc23d5192c984abc6b3fec8b2d3a56e12d8129</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-the-french-police-the-most-violent-in-the-eu/a-79732855--34f0b0f7045e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-the-french-police-the-most-violent-in-the-eu/a-79732855?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As protests continue in France, the French police are under scrutiny after new allegations of police brutality. The force has a bigger arsenal than most in Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Life near the front line in Sloviansk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24e88165ea23dfd80c3c475f9440f15092f85c7765d923049a12798a128ca4fd</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636--5ef08a6d884a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russian continues to attack Sloviansk in eastern Ukraine, thousands of residents refuse to leave or struggle to find a way out. For many, poverty, family ties and beloved pets make evacuation painfully difficult.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can Germany revive its economy before the far-right AfD gains ground?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b31350cb4f0b2f3e00eeb1b46648314e99ad8c954038f6bb5a840362abc7d5b</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-revive-its-economy-before-the-far-right-afd-gains-ground/a-79696102--ac9492c7777a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-revive-its-economy-before-the-far-right-afd-gains-ground/a-79696102?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflicts, rising costs and Chinese competition are testing Germany's economic model like never before. Can new growth sectors create jobs and ease voters' economic fears, thereby helping contain the far-right AfD?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria: Concerns about security in the Black Sea dominate presidential election campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e99fb8672589556bf7e1ffdc9ed09ab0feee9d232058b1ea12892b5666aacaa2</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094--fc0e44625feb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgaria's presidential election campaign has been shaped by recent drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea and the government's reduced support for Ukraine, making foreign policy a key factor in the first round.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: AfD's Weidel calls for major EU reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebabfbeade1b3226d94d68b7c63845a6addc372274950c59cd306544da0d7b7e</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-afd-s-weidel-calls-for-major-eu-reforms/live-79719483--29b68ddcd610.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-afd-s-weidel-calls-for-major-eu-reforms/live-79719483?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right Alternative for Germany co-leader Alice Weidel reveals the party's plan to reform the EU. Meanwhile, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang was in Berlin to talk to developers and investors. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Putin and Xi at one table, without Ukraine. What Moscow wants from the proposal and why Beijing might agree.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05691d37f446514f40bb23c6fdb1fe4ab6139227e72b4590b16f86b8c831d7f8</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-/a-79726190--eeff17927fb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-might-agree/a-79726190?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is pushing for a summit with Donald Trump and Xi Jinping to discuss ending the war in Ukraine, without Kyiv or the EU. What does Russia hope to gain, and why might China be willing to take part?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Raids at far-right group's offices at European Parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69249050e6ae701a6b8123651a1a0a61e20836bdc8863ad80fcc909a40044f8f</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631--002ed5188c2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities searched the Patriots for Europe's European Parliament offices in a long-running funding inquiry. The group says the charges pertain to its predecessor and there is "no legal continuity" between the two.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia arrests German man, calls him a Ukraine 'mercenary'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bd9a0b24fc7fa3bc31557b30da7b3ffd49c134798b7c2de20ef541422e695fe</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871--8b55608360c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian FSB agents have arrested a German national and accused him of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine's military. They claim he deserted over unpaid wages and say he was a sniper who once served in the Bundeswehr.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions target Iran's rail sector as Tehran shifts cargo from sea routes to overland corridors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d2124f9419d90abae710accb7dad48acff24928fe1b8064e59c97a92f7c323b</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-target-iran-s-rail-sector-as-tehran-shifts-cargo-from-sea-routes-to-overland-corridors/a-79681413--6d742d0c6640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-target-iran-s-rail-sector-as-tehran-shifts-cargo-from-sea-routes-to-overland-corridors/a-79681413?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As US sanctions expand to Iran's rail sector, Tehran is relying more heavily on overland links with China and Central Asia. But capacity constraints, delays and costs limit rail's ability to replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Football: German coach Hürzeler flying high in Premier League</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f609553495a8e00679460f399213dd25bfa58fb1ed9a92a9ce1a66f3990e67</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-h_rzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763--701507a044eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-hürzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fabian Hürzeler is younger than his star player, a fellow Premier League German. But, contrary to his reputation in his homeland, Hürzeler has become a popular figure both on and off the pitch in England.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Rising emissions and temperatures: The cost of Trump's climate retreat is now clear</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28bddb02f7030016a3a21eca9e02921a6f3a1a313425d8d8b8828f29e072f03d</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T05:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915--c58ce7a39bf5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-