ty's UAE owners could exit amid cheating charges. That would pose a challenge for a city — and prime minister — closely tied to Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nord Stream trial opens in Germany, defense seeks dismissal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43efef5fa69a224506dde6372ecacdcb3afe6ef56cd50a80464faceec96b0d8c</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T18:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nord-stream-trial-opens-in-germany-defense-seeks-dismissal/a-79662942--840b7e9fd757.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nord-stream-trial-opens-in-germany-defense-seeks-dismissal/a-79662942?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Serhii Kuznietsov is accused of attacking civilian infrastructure in the 2022 sabotage of the Russian gas pipeline to Germany. His lawyers called Nord Stream a military target, and said their client is sworn to secrecy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's diesel deal with Russia is unlikely to significantly lower global fuel prices despite expectations of rapid relief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95eb0503e3dd0c09dee01b206ba8d84e55712ebdcd31aacc74c41069e990b733</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia-is-unlikely-to-significantly-lower-global-fuel-prices-despite-expect/a-79659601--8934faa2519e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia-is-unlikely-to-significantly-lower-global-fuel-prices-despite-expectations-of-rapid-relief/a-79659601?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the world's largest diesel exporter, the US benefits from high prices. At home, however, consumers are feeling the strain of rising living costs. Why Donald Trump's deal with Russia is unlikely to change that.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>FIFPRO report highlights growing pains in women's football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bca6c044a1016699073dd0632ae21eaacaec02de7ea2c2233a7f7462e659768</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T08:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013--365fa34aee7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Expected global revenue of over $1 billion and new faces at the U17 World Cup show women's football is booming, but a recent report also highlights need for better structures globally.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden treasure in discarded wearable and fast tech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:619febc60d9a7a1bdbc0c9207fe52a88115151921b89bd7976a4cf3cbebff4cf</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611--7010f2eed048.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sales of fast tech like mini fans and disposable e-vapes, as well as wearable health tech such as heart monitors and smartwatches are soaring. They're creating a new e-waste problem but are full of hidden treasure.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Formula 1: Rwanda to bring sport back to Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa6fbe6e64623b326e5cdf942b58a17c1e140ce2b807340091c9416252da107d</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217--ee284b399c6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The last time Formula 1 hosted a race in Africa was way back in 1993. But a new track in Rwanda is set to host a Grand Prix in "the early 2030s," continuing the country’s investment in international sport.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c915a5261b9398990b6f01b837f2131ee85ff52fe1598951dbdd0dace144b8a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>125 years of Thomas Mann's 'Buddenbrooks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fd94d916fc60b81f9aaac5b55ffc3fc73a20b40aca6cdf4bcb1a93b7e8950c2</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236--20da98f1ab2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This over 1,000-page masterpiece offers a panoramic view of society in the 19th century and exposes the collapse of a merchant family: unrecognized sons, disillusioned daughters and the loss of middle-class ideals.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Pope lung nodule: Could it be cancer?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f49e5a900afcb12e8d6b9ebe846470f6800d0622c95a42781d5bbb57ad5aba9c</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503--9cf198017761.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The case of Pope Leo shows how small lung nodules are often found during routine health checks. Quick treatment is generally advised before nodules can grow to become larger life-threatening masses.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women: Ena Mahmutovic makes her case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28923f0ebe181b5b98e2a8cabef1582cc6e51cd3bcf5cce19d0aa0dff14be2a8</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341--71931b21638e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's win against Australia saw Ena Mahmutovic excel in goal. The 22-year-old Bayern Munich goalkeeper is considered the successor to Ann-Katrin Berger and is making a name for herself.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How green is Europe's urban public transport? A data-driven reality check</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8b031beb9d4bea7863c331e494ad4929d579ff6b8a91037de4efd76692a7fdf</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-green-is-europe-s-urban-public-transport-a-data-driven-reality-check/a-79406721--a78a7db30bc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-green-is-europe-s-urban-public-transport-a-data-driven-reality-check/a-79406721?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greener buses and cleaner fleets are reshaping public transport across Europe. But are cities moving fast enough to meet their zero-emission goals?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>UK students call for school uniforms to be banned in pornography</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2163e52487e54d226201e786773d1769e3706b07b8de93eeeb1ae9b176e105b1</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324--e21f080b6070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Short skirts, knee-high socks, white blouses: Girls' school uniform items are widely used as costumes in pornographic videos. As students experience harassment, a group wants to change that.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76ebd61ed0eb9b13e2e1fb3a27d458a30b28af5ba3b24191c7c16ed89004e68c</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af4ab47e711a9ae96f95fb95f26329ca2e3eb5b195a2c5bd26be0fdc7554dfa4</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Art for freedom: Maria Kalesnikava in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9fe52a4a24015d6bda7630994a681f873021adfdcc2372ffdf5dd655df2314b</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009--0f2314a86e67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Belarusian musician and civil rights activist Maria Kalesnikava held the keynote speech on the importance of art at the 2026 Beethovenfest in Bonn. She also visited DW.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ac4e7541e59dbe32e0b7e61bae89a431b2fd0c001b6326d316d5dee5e72656a</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948--b8b608a266b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since winning the right to hold the 2034 World Cup unopposed, Saudi Arabia has been pulling away from sport. With reports that its most ambitious stadium project will be abandoned, what does this mean for the World Cup?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Finland, the world's happiest nation, faces a glum winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f00f4b3e0736fa49f7d026af2dffc96bd885a1f98080635a7d1eacc3264c39df</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348--0df829428818.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/finland-the-world-s-happiest-nation-faces-a-glum-winter/a-79544348?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finns have many reasons to feel content, but the country's pile of debt is not one of them. Russia's war in Ukraine has added to the fiscal burden. Can the Nordic nation absorb another shock?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Nobel Prize winner Anne Carson: Where to start reading</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01a512b522810bd2874458b3a5653a2b54a3265f40fc9752539d19a3c9a9d5d8</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953--08cd2959f273.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The works of this year's Nobel Prize-winning poet and essayist Anne Carson can feel slightly daunting. Here are some keys to understanding her universe.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Early-onset cancer rising worldwide: Causes, risk, prevention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cddf3b807fc7079b33188c143796d77c4ca2e82e2313433a39a603c4853d7d0d</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097--5416293e8076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Across Latin America, early-onset cancer rates have risen, especially of bowel, breast and cervical cancers. But it is a worldwide trend.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How a multibillion-dollar oilfield has ignited the UK-Argentina feud over the Falklands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b087cdb11b328d186450e40f134ed5db11d9e7f07e746a4de2aebcbb80714335</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973--b9ae4084dbb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentina and the UK once fought a war over the Falkland Islands. Now, the multibillion-dollar Sea Lion oil project has reignited old tensions, with Buenos Aires seeking to put a stop to the plans.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature goes to Canada's Anne Carson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a68eada5e0e63a4ef60882f98af7642632c3d449c07bf79b6717bee4176fd5f2</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136--7b591c2af8dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Carson won for her "bold and inventive oeuvre." The decorated poet and essayist is known for her reverence for Latin and Greek classics.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'90s art scene in the UK: An international, edgy trendsetter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afeaccc778e15454eaa81138619b1c683f871fd5bdc2d8632f91eec3704b031d</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777--d9e1246b3502.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 1990s are remembered for Brit-pop and provocative fashion, but beyond the nostalgia, it was a decade of cultural experimentation and social change. Tate Britain's new exhibition looks past the familiar icons.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in chemistry goes to Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6930d0678d1b404a8a603a7665a9f7088339404f7b0a2126e394a34ba323107</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924--1eccf7a6b469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai won the Nobel Prize in chemistry for their groundbreaking discoveries related to the origin of chirality and life's building blocks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20169ef4795d464d9601c45890d76b18bfbae8434e1ce50a62b886a131ac60ba</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ronaldo stays on under cloud as Messi exits internationals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:541453a73e2aa5337d25ec1c322906c4758970a79a13b8879d64b6ba54f07399</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551--518c4a71824f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Just hours before Lionel Messi played his last match for Argentina, Cristiano Ronaldo posted his latest salvo in a row with Portugal. Ronaldo wants to play on despite the troubles, while Messi bathed in adulation.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nobelitis — How winning a Nobel Prize can give you delusions of grandeur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b4f3265b608d51a6a55d07e88ad117f8f8d7b0b7cae36286fa96f05f4ab919</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772--1ee420badedc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After being chosen for one of the world's most prestigious awards, some Nobel laureates lose touch with reality and suddenly start spouting unscientific nonsense. They're afflicted by what some have called "Nobelitis."</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Emerging economies are embracing solar power and skipping fossil fuels much faster than Europe or the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1fc38297532a7978aceeb1d4b27703dc858bfea58683b755693a131631924db</id><updated>2026-10-30T15:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-th/a-79474847--a24cf177c41d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-the-us/a-79474847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Renewable electricity is cheaper than ever. While the West got rich on coal and oil, some of the world's poorest countries are banking on solar, wind and water instead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title